Bug in @paperback/runtime-polyfills MockRequestManager.scheduleRequest: the
interceptor loop passes the ORIGINAL request to every interceptor instead of the
progressively-modified one, so with 2+ interceptors (the normal case: rate
limiter + cookie store) earlier mutations are silently lost.

Applied manually to node_modules after install (see aizoban#3 "Notes"):

--- a/lib/RequestManager.js
+++ b/lib/RequestManager.js
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
         let finalRequest = request;
         for (const interceptor of this.registeredInterceptors) {
             const requestInterceptor = this.selectorRegistry.selector(interceptor.interceptRequestSelectorId);
-            finalRequest = await requestInterceptor(request);
+            finalRequest = await requestInterceptor(finalRequest);
         }
